======================================================================
CONCLUSION
======================================================================
Three complementary signals per pair:
  1. Diversity counts (raw / centered): does any method cross its threshold?
  2. Spread/range of TMdiff: how much do clusters vary in fold preference?
  3. Cross-method concordance: do orthogonal methods agree per-cluster on
     direction, even if no single method crosses its threshold?

Strongest fold-switching candidates satisfy 2+ of these signals.
Cross-method concordance is least sensitive to method-specific
training bias and threshold choice.


